Introduction:


The Backend is the Webserver. Wie have the functions:

    /login
    /logout
    /refresh
    /validate/refresh-token
    /validate/access-token
    /register

For the accessToken and RefreshToken we use the JWT-Token Systems This is how the Refresh and Acces Token Look like:



Refresh:

        "sub": str(user.id),
        "admin": bool(user.admin), #Should be deleted?
        "typ": "refresh",
        "jti": jti,
        "iat": int(now.timestamp()),
        "exp": int(exp.timestamp()),

Access:

        "sub": str(user.id),
        "admin": bool(user.admin),
        "typ": "access",
        "iat": int(now.timestamp()),
        "exp": int((now + timedelta(minutes=ACCESS_MINUTES)).timestamp()),

Now we come to the REST API The Following we have:

Login
Input: {email: str, password:str} -> Output: {access_token: str, refresh_token: str, token_type: str = "bearer"}
The possible Errors are:
    1.         401 / {"invalid credentials"}
     --> If User doesnt already exists, credentials are invalid, or user is inactive


-----Authentification API ---------
Before using the Authentfication API wee need to set at least the JWT-Secret with:
%Code:
Authentificator.set_secret("")
%
Further if we want to extract user Info setting the Database-Config is necessary too:
%Code:
Authentificator.set_user_database_url("")
Authentificator.set_user_database_user("")
Authentificator.set_user_database_password("")
Authentificator.set_user_database_table("")
Authentificator.connect_database()
%
Usage in vanilla python:


1. Authentificated:
Output: true/False
Input: accesstoken
...

Usage for FastAPI-Only:

@RequireAuth(require_admin=yes/no)
async def refresh(payload: AccessIn, db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)):


async def refresh(payload: AccessIn,access_token : str, user: User, RequireUser(access_token) db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)):


async def refresh(access_token: str, AccessIn, db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)):


 The User Objects looks liek this:

     __tablename__ = "users"

    id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)
    email: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(320), unique=True, index=True)
    hashed_password: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(500))
    first_name: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(120))
    last_name: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(120))
    username: Mapped[str | None] = mapped_column(String(120), unique=True, index=True, nullable=True)
    newsletter: Mapped[bool] = mapped_column(Boolean, default=False)
    is_active: Mapped[bool] = mapped_column(Boolean, default=True)
    admin: Mapped[bool] = mapped_column(Boolean, default=False)
    created_at: Mapped[datetime] = mapped_column(DateTime(timezone=True), server_default=func.now())
    refresh_tokens: Mapped[list["RefreshToken"]] = relationship(back_populates="user", cascade="all, delete-orphan")

